        <mxCell id="rl7uGPVT0k8NYsay8ons-60" edge="1" parent="1" source="rl7uGPVT0k8NYsay8ons-18" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;curved=1;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;" target="rl7uGPVT0k8NYsay8ons-59">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="rl7uGPVT0k8NYsay8ons-65" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;strokeColor=#FF2D2D;" value="- It is unclear what the features from the&amp;nbsp; first dense feature volume represent. As such, it is also unclear how one is meant to set ane xplicit regionalized target for this step.&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- An alternative to this is to explicitly specify the regions to be filled (voxel painting or just placing rough shapes for example), and using that as initial coordinates, bypassing sparse structure generation altogether.&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="200" width="370" x="1040" y="1350" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="rl7uGPVT0k8NYsay8ons-70" edge="1" parent="1" source="rl7uGPVT0k8NYsay8ons-67" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;curved=1;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;" target="rl7uGPVT0k8NYsay8ons-69">
